      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are experiencing a deep disorientation where your sense of self was so intertwined with his presence. This feeling of emptiness is a natural, though agonizing, reaction to losing that central structure in your life. While the pain feels unending right now, please remember that emptiness can eventually soften into space, not necessarily into forgetting. Reaching out to a grief counselor or support group can provide a safe environment to help you slowly navigate this loss of self.",
